{"title":"2000 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Videos:\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Videos:</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are 5 yellow pegs, 4 red pegs, 3 green pegs, 2 blue pegs, and 1 orange peg to be placed on a triangular peg board. In how many ways can the pegs be placed so that no (horizontal) row or (vertical) column contains two pegs of the same color?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/c/f8cf7c5b851f88e9d59d30bcb4be17d962a2d001.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(20); dot((0,0)); dot((1,0)); dot((2,0)); dot((3,0)); dot((4,0)); dot((0,1)); dot((1,1)); dot((2,1)); dot((3,1)); dot((0,2)); dot((1,2)); dot((2,2)); dot((0,3)); dot((1,3)); dot((0,4)); [/asy]\" width=\"138\" height=\"138\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/a/75a8f06ec870aa032fbcad735e24b0d80e40ff83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 0 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 1 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 5!\\cdot 4!\\cdot 3!\\cdot 2!\\cdot 1!  \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{15!}{5!\\cdot 4!\\cdot 3!\\cdot 2!\\cdot 1!} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 15!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"594\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Videos:\">Videos:</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Videos:\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IP3aip6lT40\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IP3aip6lT40</a>\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Ca6WSj9NN7k?t=510\">https://youtu.be/Ca6WSj9NN7k?t=510</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In each column there must be one orange peg. In particular, in the rightmost column, there is only one peg spot, therefore an orange peg must go there. \n</p><p>In the second column from the right, there are two spaces for pegs. One of them is in the same row as the corner peg, so there is only one remaining choice left for the orange peg in this column.\n</p><p>By similar logic, we can fill in the orange pegs as shown:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/5/1a55631eca1f2268646ee2a553a6799355bcb492.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(20); dot((0,0)); dot((1,0)); dot((2,0)); dot((3,0)); label(&quot;Y&quot;,(4,-.35),N); dot((0,1)); dot((1,1)); dot((2,1)); label(&quot;Y&quot;,(3,.6),N); dot((0,2)); dot((1,2)); label(&quot;Y&quot;,(2,1.6),N); dot((0,3)); label(&quot;Y&quot;,(1,2.6),N); label(&quot;Y&quot;,(0,3.6),N); [/asy]\" width=\"155\" height=\"152\" />\n</p><p>After this we can proceed to fill in the whole pegboard, so there is only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> arrangement of the pegs. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/d/f0d5b8fdfd2bd98c8be0bad569663660c33f3438.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{B}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/5/d959956ff965f40dd2fdc86a6e3c3dc8f9223f8e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(20); label(&quot;O&quot;,(0,-.35),N); label(&quot;B&quot;,(1,-.35),N); label(&quot;G&quot;,(2,-.35),N); label(&quot;R&quot;,(3,-.35),N); label(&quot;Y&quot;,(4,-.35),N); label(&quot;B&quot;,(0,.6),N); label(&quot;G&quot;,(1,.6),N); label(&quot;R&quot;,(2,.6),N); label(&quot;Y&quot;,(3,.6),N); label(&quot;G&quot;,(0,1.6),N); label(&quot;R&quot;,(1,1.6),N); label(&quot;Y&quot;,(2,1.6),N); label(&quot;R&quot;,(0,2.6),N); label(&quot;Y&quot;,(1,2.6),N); label(&quot;Y&quot;,(0,3.6),N); [/asy]\" width=\"155\" height=\"152\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ulL-ubpVEhI?si=LCdBBXv0VL4jsM6v\">https://youtu.be/ulL-ubpVEhI?si=LCdBBXv0VL4jsM6v</a>\n</p><p>~Thesmartgreekmathdude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10\" title=\"2000 AMC 10\">2000 AMC 10</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems\" title=\"2000 AMC 10 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Answer_Key\" title=\"2000 AMC 10 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_12\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2000 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_14\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2000 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2000 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•